{:edb/db-before-t 1855 :edb/db-after-t 1856 :edb/tx-data [[13194139535168 50 #inst "2026-10-08T18:31:02.308Z" 13194139535168 true] [17592186119526 1100 "Consider the system of equations\n${5x + 2y =-1; - 3x + 3y = 9$.\nExpress $y$ in terms of $2 \\times 2$ determinants." 13194139535168 false] [17592186119526 1100 "Consider the system of equations \n\n$$\n{\\begin{aligned}5x+2y=-1 \\\\ -3x+3y=9.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nExpress $y$ in terms of $2 \\times 2$ determinants." 13194139535168 true] [17592186119526 1145 "We are given the system\n\n$$\n{5x + 2y =-1; - 3x + 3y = 9\n$$\n\nThe determinant of the coefficient matrix is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\nD &= \\begin{vmatrix}5 & 2 \\\\ -3 & 3\\end{vmatrix}\n\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow, to construct $D_y$, we replace the second column of the coefficient matrix by the right-hand side column of the given system:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\nD_{y} &= \\begin{vmatrix}5 & -1 \\\\ -3 & 9\\end{vmatrix}\n\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFinally, according to Cramer's rule, we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\ny &= \\frac{D_{y}}{D} = \\frac{\\begin{vmatrix}5 & -1 \\\\ -3 & 9\\end{vmatrix}}{\\begin{vmatrix}5 & 2 \\\\ -3 & 3\\end{vmatrix}}\n\\end{aligned}\n$$" 13194139535168 false] [17592186119526 1145 "We are given the system\n\n$$\n{\\begin{aligned}5x+2y=-1 \\\\ -3x+3y=9.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThe determinant of the coefficient matrix is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}D & =|\\begin{aligned}5 & 2 \\\\ -3 & 3\\end{aligned}|.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow, to construct $D_y$, we replace the second column of the coefficient matrix by the right-hand side column of the given system:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{D}_{y} & =|\\begin{aligned}5 & -1 \\\\ -3 & 9\\end{aligned}|\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFinally, according to Cramer's rule, we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}y & =\\frac{{D}_{y}}{D}=\\frac{|\\begin{aligned}5 & -1 \\\\ -3 & 9\\end{aligned}|}{|\\begin{aligned}5 & 2 \\\\ -3 & 3\\end{aligned}|}.\\end{aligned}\n$$" 13194139535168 true] [17592186119528 1100 "Let $\\langle x,3 \\rangle$ be the solution of the system of equations below.\n${5x - 2y = 4; x + ky = 8$\nWhich of the following equations could be solved to find the value of $k$?\n\n1. $\\begin{vmatrix}5 & -2 \\\\ 1 & k\\end{vmatrix}$\n2. $\\begin{vmatrix}5 & -2 \\\\ 1 & k\\end{vmatrix}$\n3. $\\begin{vmatrix}5 & -2 \\\\ 1 & k\\end{vmatrix}$" 13194139535168 false] [17592186119528 1100 "Let $\\langle x,3 \\rangle$ be the solution of the system of equations below. \n\n$$\n{\\begin{aligned}5x-2y=4 \\\\ x+ky=8\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nWhich of the following equations could be solved to find the value of $k?$\n\n- ![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14057622/assets/b82f5c43c9ec788b95e7213bef63eb37e4abf9d0159f92cbeedc0f64c4d35283.png)\n\n- ![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14057622/assets/648ce0c1b8b77c1230c6c634c676624f9c79c12ffc3942abc09d24d0fdc424d3.png)\n\n- ![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14057622/assets/bc7a566778813050611b098cebe221aa77ac27677e922cd282fc8ff9c3670cfd.png)" 13194139535168 true] [17592186119528 1145 "The determinant of the coefficient matrix is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\nD &= \\begin{vmatrix}5 & -2 \\\\ 1 & k\\end{vmatrix}\n\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nAccording to Cramer's rule, the value of $y$ is given by\n\n$$\ny=\\dfrac{D_y}{D}\n$$\n\nwhere\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\nD_{y} &= \\begin{vmatrix}5 & 4 \\\\ 1 & 8\\end{vmatrix} \\\\\n&= 5 \\cdot 8 - 4 \\cdot 1 \\\\\n&= 36\n\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\ny &= \\frac{D_{y}}{D} \\\\\n3 &= \\frac{36}{\\begin{vmatrix}5 & -2 \\\\ 1 & k\\end{vmatrix}} \\\\\n\\begin{vmatrix}5 & -2 \\\\ 1 & k\\end{vmatrix} &= 12\n\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSo, the correct answer is \"II only\"." 13194139535168 false] [17592186119528 1145 "The determinant of the coefficient matrix is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}D & =|\\begin{aligned}5 & -2 \\\\ 1 & k\\end{align